<title>INDIA: India RBI allows firms to swap rupees for forex.</title>
<headline>India RBI allows firms to swap rupees for forex.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian companies can swap rupee funds for foreign currency without prior approval of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI), the central bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It also allowed Indian corporate exporters and importers forward cover without documentary evidence of a firm order.</p>
<p>The RBI announced the looser regulations as part of the RBI's credit policy for the first half fiscal 1997/98 (April-March).</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
